GRANT Of ACCESS EASEMENT
KNOW ALL MEN BY THESE PRESENTS that, for and in consideration ofthe sum ofOne
Dollar ($1.00) and other valuable considerations in hand paid, the receipt and adequacy of which
is hereby acknowledged, the CITY OF CHEYENNE, a municipal corporation organized under the
laws of the State of Wyoming, 2101 O’Neil Avenue, Cheyenne, Wyoming 82001, hereinafter
referred to as GRANTOR, does hereby grant, remise and relinquish unto JOSEPH M.DYSON,
Trustee of the Dyson Family Trust dated October 29, 1979, and to his successors in trust, $53
Tamalpais Avenue, Apartment C2 11, Novato, California 94947, hereinafter referred to as
GRANTEE, the non-exclusive right, privilege, authority and easement for use and maintenance of
an access road across lands owned by GRANTOR, or in which GRANTOR has any interest, further
described as follows:
LEGAL DESCRIPTION
A 60 foot wide access easement on an existing gravel road, being in the NE1/4NE1/4
of Section 23, Township 13 North, Range 68 West, of the 6th P.M., in Laramie
County, Wyoming, being 30 feet either side of the following described centerline:
Beginning at the Northeast corner ofsaid Section 23, thence S. 89°45 ‘44” W., along
the Northerly line of said Section 23 a distance of 308.56 feet to the true point of
beginning for this easement;
Thence S. 48°01’07” W., adistance of 411.37 feetto apoint;
Thence S. 38°58’47” W., a distance of66.45 feet to a point on the Northerly right of
way line of Wyoming State Highway No.225 (Otto Road);
Said parcel containing 0.66 acre more or less.
SEE EXHIBIT “A” ACCOMPANYING.
GRANTOR further covenants that it shall, in no way, hinder or prevent the proper and
reasonable use and enjoyment of said property for access by GRANTEE, its successors, assigns,
lessees, invitees and agents.
The rights granted herein shall forever be subject to the rights of GRANTOR, its assigns or
lessees to explore for, develop, and extract any and all minerals or other subsurface resources
beneath this easement.
Upon abandonment or discontinuance of use of this easement for the purposes specified
above, all of GRANTEE’S rights under this grant of easement shall revert to GRANTOR or its
assigns, the same as if this grant had never been made. Should this easement be abandoned by the
GRANTEE, or GRANTEE’S successors or assigns, the above described tract of land shall be
returned to a condition satisfactory to the landowner.
The easement may be transferred; however, no transfer may increase the burden on the
servient estate in any manner.
Any transfer ofownership ofthis easement, or any change ofname or mailing address ofthe
owner of this easement, shall be reported to the GRANTOR within thirty (30) days of the transfer
or change.
